* The webhook is marked as processed before any side effects run. If processing throws (DB error, hook error, timeout), Stripe will retry with the same event id but `alreadyProcessed()` will return true and the retry will be skipped—permanently dropping the event and leaving the system out of sync. Fix by making idempotency a transactional claim: insert an event row as a 'processing' claim inside the same DB transaction as the subscription updates, and only mark it processed (e.g., set `processedAt`) after successful completion; on failure, roll back (or delete/unset the claim) so retries can re-run.
